WEBVTT

00:00:05.590 --> 00:00:07.980
It's a promise, Kaito.

00:00:08.830 --> 00:00:10.820
It's not the puzzle that's bad.

00:00:10.820 --> 00:00:12.310
The one who betrays you is always

00:00:12.310 --> 00:00:13.990
the human who made it.

00:00:14.960 --> 00:00:17.510
Let's believe, you and me.

00:00:17.510 --> 00:00:18.960
In puzzles.

00:00:18.960 --> 00:00:19.880
Yeah.

00:00:21.160 --> 00:00:23.420
<i>It's a promise. For both of us.</i>

00:00:24.180 --> 00:00:26.280
Yeah. It's a promise.

00:00:32.580 --> 00:00:33.640
Rook...

00:00:33.930 --> 00:00:35.130
Calling me?

00:00:37.750 --> 00:00:38.900
Upperclassman Jikukawa!

00:00:38.900 --> 00:00:39.640
How long have you...?

00:00:40.050 --> 00:00:41.640
How long, indeed?

00:00:42.130 --> 00:00:43.650
You want something?

00:00:43.650 --> 00:00:48.060
We've got another request for
you to solve a new puzzle.

00:00:48.060 --> 00:00:50.010
Leave some Sunday open, okay?

00:00:53.050 --> 00:00:53.860
Kaito?

00:00:54.540 --> 00:00:56.010
Cut the crap.

00:00:56.010 --> 00:00:58.650
Philosopher's Puzzles and
prizes or whatever

00:00:58.650 --> 00:00:59.950
have nothin' to do with me.

00:01:01.160 --> 00:01:02.200
Yes, I know.

00:01:03.120 --> 00:01:05.210
I thought this particular puzzle might

00:01:05.210 --> 00:01:07.350
be impossible even for you,

00:01:07.350 --> 00:01:08.700
but... Oh, well.

00:01:08.700 --> 00:01:09.580
See you.

00:01:11.410 --> 00:01:13.090
What kind of puzzle is it?

00:01:13.940 --> 00:01:15.370
Thank goodness.

00:01:15.370 --> 00:01:17.760
I thought you might do it for us, Kaito.

00:01:18.090 --> 00:01:20.270
I-I haven't said I'll do it y-

00:01:20.270 --> 00:01:23.450
I thought you'd need a
partner for this puzzle,

00:01:23.450 --> 00:01:24.930
so I've readied one for you.

00:01:24.930 --> 00:01:26.640
A partner? The heck?

00:01:27.220 --> 00:01:30.360
Go to Art Room No. 2
if you want to meet...

00:01:30.360 --> 00:01:33.150
the person given the title of Da Vinci.

00:01:33.920 --> 00:01:35.240
Da Vinci?

00:02:05.600 --> 00:02:07.910
Kimi no nounai e to shinnyuu
Gonna infiltrate your brain

00:02:07.910 --> 00:02:10.640
Nemutteru suki ni baby, open the gate
While you're sleeping, baby, open the gate

00:02:10.640 --> 00:02:12.490
Fukuzatsusugi security
Too-complicated security

00:02:12.490 --> 00:02:15.230
Kakusareru to abakitakunaru
When something's hidden, it makes me want to expose it

00:02:15.230 --> 00:02:19.740
Barabara ni chirabatte iru password o hiroiatsume
I'll gather up those loose, scattered passwords

00:02:19.740 --> 00:02:24.450
Kakushin ni sematte yuku, sono shoutai o misete
And approach the core, so show me that true form

00:02:24.450 --> 00:02:26.670
Kantan ni clear dekinai
I can't clear it easily

00:02:26.670 --> 00:02:29.320
Saki nante motto yomenai
Can read what lies ahead even less

00:02:29.320 --> 00:02:31.330
Kaidoku fukanou smile
A smile that can't be deciphered

00:02:31.330 --> 00:02:33.630
Kiken na puzzle
A dangerous puzzle

00:02:33.630 --> 00:02:35.570
Lock sareteta door aru nara
If there's a door that's been locked

00:02:35.570 --> 00:02:38.390
Zutto tataite miru beki, kaza-ana hiraku wa
You must keep striking it, a crack will open

00:02:38.390 --> 00:02:42.890
Eien ni hodokenai nazo nanka wa nai
No mystery remains unsolved forever

00:02:42.890 --> 00:02:45.190
Makiokosu, it's a supernova!
It's forming, it's a supernova!

00:02:45.190 --> 00:02:49.880
Tobikiri shigekiteki na hirameki o agemashou
I will give you thoroughly stimulating insight

00:02:49.880 --> 00:02:52.100
Misskey-misskey la-tu-ma

00:02:52.100 --> 00:02:54.440
Yume no naka, it's a supernova!
In the middle of a dream, it's a supernova!

00:02:54.440 --> 00:02:57.070
Watashi wa, sou, brain diver
I am, yes, a brain diver

00:02:57.070 --> 00:03:02.960
Kimi ga sagashimotometeru kotae ni nareru made
Until I become familiar with the answer you seek

00:03:05.620 --> 00:03:08.640
Brain diver

00:03:10.370 --> 00:03:13.440
Brain diver

00:03:18.030 --> 00:03:21.950
The Girl in the Closed Room

00:03:28.400 --> 00:03:30.980
Sunday, huh? What should we do?

00:03:31.550 --> 00:03:35.980
The Softball Club asked
me to help out that day...

00:03:35.980 --> 00:03:38.520
Why are YOU worryin' about this?

00:03:38.520 --> 00:03:40.450
Oh! True enough,

00:03:40.450 --> 00:03:41.760
it might be good to have a

00:03:41.760 --> 00:03:43.760
partner other than me once in a while.

00:03:43.760 --> 00:03:45.950
I told you, I'm gonna
go say "No," didn't I?

00:03:45.950 --> 00:03:50.000
And anyway, since when
have you been my partner?

00:03:50.270 --> 00:03:52.750
Yeah... At this rate, you'll never be

00:03:52.750 --> 00:03:55.580
able to leave Nonoha's nest, huh?

00:03:55.580 --> 00:03:59.590
Why are you talkin' like
you're some laboring parent?!

00:03:59.610 --> 00:04:03.290
Kaito and Nonoha look
like they're having fun.

00:04:03.290 --> 00:04:07.100
I have to use puzzles to up my own appeal!

00:04:08.060 --> 00:04:10.340
This is kinda spooky...

00:04:11.290 --> 00:04:13.100
Art Room No. 2

00:04:14.560 --> 00:04:16.500
There won't be any ghosts
or anything, right?

00:04:16.500 --> 00:04:17.650
Cut it out.

00:04:24.930 --> 00:04:26.640
Wh-What's that?!

00:04:26.640 --> 00:04:28.780
Don't tell me it's a g-g...

00:04:30.540 --> 00:04:31.870
Hey, Kaito!

00:04:44.090 --> 00:04:45.350
Kaito!

00:04:49.790 --> 00:04:52.130
Huh? A girl?

00:04:52.130 --> 00:04:54.140
I, Ana, think...

00:04:54.140 --> 00:04:58.520
you shouldn't disturb the
birds while they're talking.

00:05:02.060 --> 00:05:03.720
That's enough for today.

00:05:03.720 --> 00:05:04.820
You think so, right?

00:05:04.820 --> 00:05:06.040
What do you mean, "right?"

00:05:06.630 --> 00:05:07.540
Right?

00:05:07.540 --> 00:05:08.560
Beats me.

00:05:14.290 --> 00:05:16.000
No!

00:05:17.890 --> 00:05:20.130
My eyes... My eyes!

00:05:20.130 --> 00:05:21.170
I just remembered.

00:05:21.970 --> 00:05:23.650
There was a rumor about a student

00:05:23.650 --> 00:05:25.720
who never came to class,

00:05:25.720 --> 00:05:27.590
just stayed inside the art room.

00:05:28.150 --> 00:05:31.220
They say she had incredible
artistic ability.

00:05:32.050 --> 00:05:35.470
Her name was... Ana Gram.

00:05:35.470 --> 00:05:36.840
Ana Gram?

00:05:37.620 --> 00:05:39.500
That's who this "Da Vinci" is?

00:05:39.500 --> 00:05:41.800
Kaito!

00:05:41.800 --> 00:05:45.300
This jigsaw puzzle was too hard for me!

00:05:45.300 --> 00:05:46.950
Maybe we could do it tog-

00:05:49.460 --> 00:05:50.610
Oh, dear.

00:05:50.610 --> 00:05:52.500
-Ah, Leo-Leo!

00:05:52.490 --> 00:05:53.330
-Leo-Leo?

00:05:53.920 --> 00:05:56.480
This puzzle is a picture
of Leonardo Da Vinci's.

00:05:56.480 --> 00:05:58.170
I, Ana, love Leo-Leo!

00:05:58.630 --> 00:06:00.510
You recognized the picture even though

00:06:00.510 --> 00:06:02.430
the pieces are scattered?

00:06:02.430 --> 00:06:05.590
You put the puzzle together
in your head that fast?

00:06:05.590 --> 00:06:09.080
Still, I don't think this jigsaw
puzzle can be completed.

00:06:10.310 --> 00:06:12.210
There's one piece missing.

00:06:13.130 --> 00:06:15.110
Actually, that's true!

00:06:15.110 --> 00:06:17.140
You knew THAT, too?

00:06:17.140 --> 00:06:19.980
This girl's a super fan of puzzles, huh?

00:06:20.300 --> 00:06:21.640
Puzzles?

00:06:21.640 --> 00:06:24.570
Hm. I'm not so interested in them, maybe.

00:06:25.310 --> 00:06:28.740
But I'm VERY interested
in Schwa-Schwa paintings!

00:06:29.000 --> 00:06:30.320
Schwa-Schwa?

00:06:30.320 --> 00:06:31.240
The heck is that?

00:06:32.490 --> 00:06:35.820
Schwarzenberg. Souji said that...

00:06:35.820 --> 00:06:39.000
I, Ana, and Kaito would go
to Schwarzenberg's house.

00:06:39.200 --> 00:06:41.880
Now listen, you're sounding
too chummy about Kaito-

00:06:41.880 --> 00:06:45.640
I, Ana, am looking forward
to it, next Sunday!

00:06:46.800 --> 00:06:51.260
Yeah, about that, I don't feel
like goin' with you at all.

00:06:51.650 --> 00:06:54.810
I understand. I'll go alone.

00:06:54.810 --> 00:06:56.200
No, you won't.

00:06:56.200 --> 00:06:59.050
Puzzles with prizes
sealed inside them are dangerous.

00:06:59.880 --> 00:07:01.230
I will be careful.

00:07:01.450 --> 00:07:03.520
No, I'm going alone!

00:07:03.520 --> 00:07:04.620
Why?

00:07:04.620 --> 00:07:07.030
I don't need some partner.

00:07:07.030 --> 00:07:10.300
I can do it on my own. Got it?

00:07:12.330 --> 00:07:13.760
So I'll meet you there!

00:07:14.420 --> 00:07:16.880
Are you even listening?

00:07:16.880 --> 00:07:18.500
I, Ana, don't need a partner.

00:07:18.860 --> 00:07:21.160
YOU'RE the partner, right?!

00:07:21.160 --> 00:07:23.320
You'd get in the way of
me solvin' the puzzle.

00:07:23.320 --> 00:07:26.100
I won't do the puzzle. I'll
just look at the paintings.

00:07:26.100 --> 00:07:27.840
<i>-She's not listening. </i>

00:07:26.100 --> 00:07:27.840
-That would get in the way!

00:07:27.840 --> 00:07:30.660
<i>-A cute girl like that, as his partner...</i>

00:07:27.840 --> 00:07:30.700
-Schwa-Schwa belongs to everyone.

00:07:30.700 --> 00:07:32.930
Schwa-Schwa's got nothin' to do with it!

00:07:32.930 --> 00:07:34.660
Kaito, are you tired?

00:07:34.660 --> 00:07:36.420
And whose fault is that?!

00:07:39.050 --> 00:07:40.260
<i>Right about now...</i>

00:07:40.730 --> 00:07:42.230
<i>He and that girl...</i>

00:07:42.230 --> 00:07:43.730
<i>Together, alone!</i>

00:07:44.320 --> 00:07:46.730
<i>Yes, it would be bad.</i>

00:07:49.290 --> 00:07:51.110
That's a big-ass mansion.

00:07:51.110 --> 00:07:54.700
I, Ana, think that as
Schwa-Schwa's house,

00:07:54.700 --> 00:07:55.950
of course it is!

00:07:56.440 --> 00:07:57.260
The heck?

00:07:57.260 --> 00:07:58.550
F'friends!

00:07:58.550 --> 00:08:00.090
"F'friends"?

00:08:00.090 --> 00:08:01.790
Feline friends.

00:08:02.850 --> 00:08:04.640
I'LL solve the puzzle.

00:08:04.640 --> 00:08:06.540
Don't go buttin' in or anything.

00:08:06.840 --> 00:08:08.480
I won't.

00:08:13.270 --> 00:08:16.550
Welcome. We have been expecting you.

00:08:17.960 --> 00:08:19.240
Please, this way.

00:08:19.240 --> 00:08:20.060
Thanks.

00:08:20.570 --> 00:08:22.240
A Schwa-Schwa painting!

00:08:22.240 --> 00:08:23.340
Hey!

00:08:26.650 --> 00:08:29.420
Yeah, I should've left her behind.

00:08:30.490 --> 00:08:31.760
Honestly!

00:08:31.760 --> 00:08:34.100
How long do you intend
to keep me waiting?

00:08:37.820 --> 00:08:42.860
Presenting the family head,
Madam Laura Frederica Schwarzenberg.

00:08:42.860 --> 00:08:46.330
You two are students at Baron's school?

00:08:46.720 --> 00:08:49.620
You don't appear very bright.

00:08:50.790 --> 00:08:52.580
No matter.

00:08:52.580 --> 00:08:55.750
If you can solve it, please
hurry up and do so.

00:09:02.960 --> 00:09:05.990
That old lady is
Schwarzenberg the painter?

00:09:05.990 --> 00:09:07.050
No.

00:09:07.050 --> 00:09:08.610
My husband has passed on.

00:09:08.610 --> 00:09:10.730
Last month, in a plane accident.

00:09:12.210 --> 00:09:14.700
He was a great man.

00:09:14.700 --> 00:09:18.300
He was a boring man, with
no talent but for painting.

00:09:18.740 --> 00:09:21.700
He was a great painter of
landscapes or some such,

00:09:22.120 --> 00:09:24.060
flying around the world looking for

00:09:24.060 --> 00:09:26.090
his so-called "subject matter".

00:09:26.090 --> 00:09:28.580
He would return just
once or twice a year.

00:09:28.780 --> 00:09:34.030
To me, he's no different
dead than he was alive.

00:09:34.030 --> 00:09:35.890
He was your husband, right?

00:09:35.890 --> 00:09:38.550
Talkin' about the dead that way...

00:09:39.150 --> 00:09:41.970
You know nothing about that man!

00:09:44.890 --> 00:09:49.810
Please note, the Madam is kind
but has something of a temper.

00:09:51.480 --> 00:09:52.570
I think...

00:09:53.220 --> 00:09:55.150
His paintings are quite lovely.

00:09:55.880 --> 00:09:57.800
And that is all.

00:09:59.230 --> 00:10:04.430
Madam Laura has inherited
this mansion, but...

00:10:04.430 --> 00:10:06.660
I'm going to sell it.

00:10:07.100 --> 00:10:09.490
Most unfortunate.

00:10:10.260 --> 00:10:12.960
Unfortunate, is it? This mansion...

00:10:13.750 --> 00:10:17.060
Has not a single good memory to offer.

00:10:18.630 --> 00:10:21.710
However, before passing
it to someone else,

00:10:21.710 --> 00:10:25.590
the puzzle containing
the prize left behind

00:10:25.590 --> 00:10:28.100
by the Master must be solved.

00:10:29.630 --> 00:10:31.270
Please, come this way.

00:10:43.790 --> 00:10:47.540
<i>The prize is sealed
inside the safe within.</i>

00:10:47.800 --> 00:10:49.460
And what is this prize?

00:10:49.460 --> 00:10:53.790
That man died having
said nothing about it.

00:10:54.260 --> 00:10:58.380
You two will, of course,
receive your share.

00:10:58.380 --> 00:11:00.340
Will 20% suffice?

00:11:00.340 --> 00:11:02.990
I'm sure it's nothing
worthwhile, after all.

00:11:02.990 --> 00:11:04.460
No, Madam.

00:11:04.460 --> 00:11:09.560
The prize that the Master
left behind is most valuable indeed.

00:11:10.060 --> 00:11:12.060
Sebastian! You...

00:11:12.550 --> 00:11:15.450
Yes, I know what it is.

00:11:15.450 --> 00:11:19.950
The reason for that is, by
the Master's instruction...

00:11:21.190 --> 00:11:24.070
it was I who built this puzzle.

00:11:28.000 --> 00:11:30.500
So then you're the...!

00:11:30.900 --> 00:11:36.000
Yes. I am the POG's Giver.

00:11:42.910 --> 00:11:45.910
<i>This wall shall not
reopen until you release</i>

00:11:45.910 --> 00:11:50.000
<i>
the prize sealed within the safe.</i>

00:11:50.000 --> 00:11:53.390
So, I take it we have been trapped?

00:11:53.390 --> 00:11:55.230
I told you not to come, didn't I?!

00:11:55.230 --> 00:11:56.370
<i>In addition...</i>

00:12:00.740 --> 00:12:01.640
Gas?!

00:12:01.640 --> 00:12:05.410
<i>That gas is heavier than air,
so it shall pool downward.</i>

00:12:05.700 --> 00:12:08.330
<i>In other words, your
time limit is however</i>

00:12:08.330 --> 00:12:11.410
<i>long it takes for you
to sink to its bottom.</i>

00:12:14.000 --> 00:12:16.210
A puzzle that toys with our lives...!

00:12:16.760 --> 00:12:20.070
<i>What IS known is that, going
forward, you will be a</i>

00:12:20.070 --> 00:12:23.080
<i>Solver and you will fight
the Givers of the POG.</i>

00:12:23.080 --> 00:12:25.550
<i>Rather, I would ask that you do so.</i>

00:12:27.960 --> 00:12:30.300
<i>The POG... I won't forgive them!</i>

00:12:30.300 --> 00:12:31.290
Kaito?

00:12:31.780 --> 00:12:32.640
First...

00:12:33.840 --> 00:12:36.690
We find WHAT in this room is the puzzle!

00:12:38.040 --> 00:12:40.300
What is the meaning of this, Sebastian?

00:12:40.300 --> 00:12:42.440
Let the two of them out this instant!

00:12:42.440 --> 00:12:44.300
Regretably...

00:12:45.400 --> 00:12:48.540
I cannot allow even you, Madam,

00:12:48.540 --> 00:12:51.200
to stand in the way of my duty!

00:12:53.160 --> 00:12:57.160
However, if you are
determined for it to be so,

00:12:57.160 --> 00:13:01.710
you may indeed save them both, Madam.

00:13:03.470 --> 00:13:07.580
Did the Master not say as such before?

00:13:07.580 --> 00:13:10.490
You may not know the puzzle,

00:13:10.490 --> 00:13:13.020
but you know the secret number.

00:13:13.020 --> 00:13:15.060
I know no such number!

00:13:15.540 --> 00:13:17.090
Truly?

00:13:18.680 --> 00:13:20.940
Could it be that you've forgotten?

00:13:24.100 --> 00:13:26.950
Okay, I'm sort of in a
hurry, so I'll be off!

00:13:29.850 --> 00:13:31.950
<i>He's in trouble! That
Philosopher's Puzzle...</i>

00:13:32.470 --> 00:13:34.540
<i>More to the point, Ana Gram!</i>

00:13:34.910 --> 00:13:36.820
<i>She's beautiful, has fashion</i>

00:13:36.330 --> 00:13:40.500
-Yo, are you for real?!

00:13:36.820 --> 00:13:38.140
<i>sense and great skin!</i>

00:13:40.500 --> 00:13:44.550
Dude! Yeah, that rocks! It rocks!

00:13:42.470 --> 00:13:44.550
-How lucky!

00:13:45.610 --> 00:13:49.550
Kaito's solving a Philosopher's Puzzle?!

00:13:49.900 --> 00:13:50.950
That's right.

00:13:50.950 --> 00:13:54.560
Why didn't friggin' upperclassman
Jikukawa ask ME, too?!

00:13:55.050 --> 00:13:57.990
In any case, if we don't hurry,
it could get dangerous.

00:13:57.990 --> 00:14:00.060
Dangerous? What kinda danger?

00:14:00.580 --> 00:14:03.210
N-Nothing at all! Hurry!

00:14:03.980 --> 00:14:06.620
Oh, this is one of Mr. Laur's paintings!

00:14:06.620 --> 00:14:09.410
And Miche! Oh, and Leb-Leb!

00:14:09.410 --> 00:14:10.740
<i>A puzzle where you get</i>

00:14:10.740 --> 00:14:13.500
the secret number from 15 paintings, huh?<i></i>

00:14:13.500 --> 00:14:16.550
<i>I don't think there's an order
to how these paintings are lined up.</i>

00:14:16.550 --> 00:14:17.830
If that's the case...

00:14:20.300 --> 00:14:21.870
The pattern of these frames!

00:14:22.850 --> 00:14:27.010
<i>They look the same,
but the wave pattern is different.</i>

00:14:27.010 --> 00:14:29.580
<i>I get it. Maybe...</i>

00:14:33.840 --> 00:14:35.530
Sure enough, they come off.

00:14:35.530 --> 00:14:37.600
Ana! Take the paintings off the walls!

00:14:37.990 --> 00:14:39.590
Huh? All of them?

00:14:39.590 --> 00:14:41.970
Yes. Hurry, there's no time!

00:14:41.970 --> 00:14:43.610
Okay. Understood.

00:14:47.030 --> 00:14:49.320
Why won't anyone answer?

00:14:50.290 --> 00:14:51.120
That's suspicious.

00:14:51.980 --> 00:14:54.620
Maybe we can see inside
if we go round back!

00:14:54.620 --> 00:14:57.180
Hey, peeping is a bad idea.

00:14:57.180 --> 00:14:58.410
I told you it was dangerous.

00:14:58.410 --> 00:14:59.370
Come on!

00:15:01.220 --> 00:15:04.040
Hey, that's too rough! Too rough!

00:15:05.120 --> 00:15:07.950
These three paintings
couldn't be removed.

00:15:07.950 --> 00:15:09.920
With these as our guide,

00:15:09.920 --> 00:15:14.100
we've lined up
paintings with the same frame pattern.

00:15:15.930 --> 00:15:18.170
This ain't the time for
you to come forward.

00:15:43.580 --> 00:15:44.420
Yes!

00:15:45.410 --> 00:15:48.290
Ana! Put arms-folded chick
there in the middle!

00:15:49.960 --> 00:15:51.290
This goes here.

00:15:51.880 --> 00:15:54.050
Mr. Corot, you go in the middle.

00:15:55.840 --> 00:15:56.930
Okay.

00:16:02.720 --> 00:16:05.180
We've lined them all up by pattern!

00:16:05.180 --> 00:16:06.680
And what does it tell us?

00:16:06.680 --> 00:16:09.960
Miche, Manet-Manet, Mill-Mill,

00:16:09.960 --> 00:16:13.060
Dr. Düre, Dora and Do-Do,

00:16:13.060 --> 00:16:15.880
Carava, Colo, Mr. Cool,

00:16:15.880 --> 00:16:16.830
Leb-Leb...

00:16:16.830 --> 00:16:17.620
Oh!

00:16:18.070 --> 00:16:18.950
Huh?

00:16:19.290 --> 00:16:22.640
I get it now, why you
were made my partner.

00:16:22.640 --> 00:16:24.870
The initials of each of the artists.

00:16:26.380 --> 00:16:27.290
Oh!

00:16:27.580 --> 00:16:32.800
From the left, M, D, C, L, V.

00:16:32.800 --> 00:16:34.330
We did it!

00:16:33.270 --> 00:16:34.330
-Yes!

00:16:35.000 --> 00:16:36.100
Huh?

00:16:36.840 --> 00:16:39.560
I guess you can't input letters.

00:16:41.520 --> 00:16:44.060
Too bad. What do we do?

00:16:44.660 --> 00:16:46.040
I don't know.

00:16:46.600 --> 00:16:48.910
Dammit! This thing...

00:16:48.910 --> 00:16:51.870
This puzzle wants to be solved!

00:16:53.540 --> 00:16:54.730
You know that?

00:16:54.730 --> 00:16:56.120
What the puzzle feels?

00:16:56.640 --> 00:17:00.560
This puzzle is very kind, and warm.

00:17:00.560 --> 00:17:03.440
That lady spoke badly about her husband,

00:17:03.440 --> 00:17:04.920
but I don't believe it!

00:17:05.430 --> 00:17:08.230
Kaito, you really like
puzzles, don't you?

00:17:08.880 --> 00:17:10.640
I made a promise:

00:17:10.640 --> 00:17:13.420
that I would trust the puzzles.

00:17:13.900 --> 00:17:16.680
<i>Let's believe, you and me.</i>

00:17:18.120 --> 00:17:19.630
<i>In puzzles.</i>

00:17:20.860 --> 00:17:26.120
But somehow, the truth
is... you despise puzzles.

00:17:26.120 --> 00:17:29.230
Isn't that what lies beneath the surface?

00:17:29.230 --> 00:17:30.750
That's the feeling I get.

00:17:37.250 --> 00:17:39.880
Dammit. Out of time.

00:17:44.580 --> 00:17:46.570
You okay? Tell me if it's too much.

00:17:46.570 --> 00:17:49.370
It ain't too much! So, what's up?

00:17:49.370 --> 00:17:52.370
It's no good. I can't
tell where Kaito is.

00:17:52.370 --> 00:17:54.170
Let's go farther that way.

00:17:54.170 --> 00:17:55.130
Okay.

00:17:55.820 --> 00:17:57.020
Dammit!

00:17:57.020 --> 00:17:57.930
Are you okay?

00:17:57.930 --> 00:17:59.050
I'm okay!

00:17:59.720 --> 00:18:03.200
Yeah, I can't tell. Let's go back.

00:18:04.980 --> 00:18:06.870
Really, tell me if it's too much.

00:18:06.870 --> 00:18:08.740
It ain't too much!

00:18:13.460 --> 00:18:15.650
I-It ain't too much at all!

00:18:17.350 --> 00:18:20.060
Ana, that third painting
that wouldn't move:

00:18:20.060 --> 00:18:21.990
Where was the painter from?

00:18:22.310 --> 00:18:24.240
Huh? Italy.

00:18:24.590 --> 00:18:26.990
I knew it. Roman numerals, huh?

00:18:26.990 --> 00:18:28.250
Roman numerals?

00:18:28.540 --> 00:18:31.840
In Roman numerals, M is 1,000,

00:18:31.840 --> 00:18:36.180
D is 500, C is 100, L is 50,

00:18:36.180 --> 00:18:38.220
and V is 5.

00:18:38.570 --> 00:18:40.890
Put them together and that makes...!

00:18:52.130 --> 00:18:54.610
Are you two all right?

00:18:54.900 --> 00:18:57.070
Yeah. We solved the puzzle.

00:18:57.070 --> 00:18:59.860
The safe's combination is 1655.

00:19:10.530 --> 00:19:13.290
THIS was his treasure?

00:19:15.740 --> 00:19:19.640
This is the last painting
the Master worked on.

00:19:20.960 --> 00:19:23.680
He would always watch me, wouldn't he?

00:19:24.340 --> 00:19:26.030
That man...

00:19:29.530 --> 00:19:31.590
It was at a small bistro in Paris.

00:19:31.590 --> 00:19:34.720
I worked there, and he was a customer.

00:19:36.290 --> 00:19:38.060
He never had any money,

00:19:38.060 --> 00:19:40.630
and would order the
cheapest things on the menu.

00:19:40.630 --> 00:19:42.490
That was every day.

00:19:43.520 --> 00:19:47.220
But once, he didn't
come for several days.

00:19:48.280 --> 00:19:51.290
I worried, thinking he might
be ill, and went to visit

00:19:51.290 --> 00:19:54.730
his atelier, carrying his favorite menu items.

00:19:54.730 --> 00:19:55.940
And when I did...

00:19:56.990 --> 00:19:59.310
That man was the picture of health,

00:19:59.310 --> 00:20:01.190
with a picture of me at his side.

00:20:01.600 --> 00:20:03.820
"I was sure you'd come," he said,

00:20:03.820 --> 00:20:06.470
grinning like a prank-loving child.

00:20:07.950 --> 00:20:11.380
I was so surprised, I
forgot that I was angry...

00:20:12.040 --> 00:20:14.270
I fell in love.

00:20:14.850 --> 00:20:18.090
That place of memories,
where he and I were bound together...

00:20:18.720 --> 00:20:20.780
That memorable number.

00:20:21.230 --> 00:20:23.440
It's a story from my youth.

00:20:23.440 --> 00:20:26.370
A story from long, long ago.

00:20:27.160 --> 00:20:29.960
Kaito, Ana, excellently done.

00:20:29.960 --> 00:20:31.930
By vocation, I may be a Giver,

00:20:31.930 --> 00:20:34.610
but I offer my sincerest apologies.

00:20:34.610 --> 00:20:37.250
They solved the puzzle, thank goodness,

00:20:37.250 --> 00:20:39.390
but using poison gas on them...

00:20:39.390 --> 00:20:41.720
Who said that was poison gas?

00:20:43.450 --> 00:20:46.520
It was theatrical smoke.

00:20:46.520 --> 00:20:51.010
After all, the Master was
quite fond of practical jokes.

00:20:53.300 --> 00:20:56.020
Your puzzle had a kind warmth.

00:20:56.020 --> 00:20:59.190
The POG has different kinds of Givers, huh?

00:21:00.020 --> 00:21:03.030
I merely made the puzzle

00:21:03.030 --> 00:21:06.450
according to the wishes of the client.

00:21:12.550 --> 00:21:14.830
What's with that satisfied-looking face?

00:21:15.310 --> 00:21:18.340
Huh? What are you two doing here?

00:21:18.820 --> 00:21:20.640
Th-That's got nothing to
do with you, does it?!

00:21:21.050 --> 00:21:23.730
Sure looks like nothing at all, huh?

00:21:23.730 --> 00:21:26.180
Nonoha, if you like, I could show you home-

00:21:26.180 --> 00:21:27.890
Ana, did you have fun?

00:21:27.890 --> 00:21:31.700
Yes. I, Ana, think it was a lot of fun!

00:21:31.700 --> 00:21:33.620
Huh. And you, Kaito?

00:21:33.620 --> 00:21:36.150
Yeah, been a while since
I've felt this good.

00:21:40.510 --> 00:21:42.140
What shall we do?

00:21:44.490 --> 00:21:45.940
It's nothing to be concerned about.

00:21:46.910 --> 00:21:49.450
Now we wait and see, yes?

00:21:51.510 --> 00:21:54.060
It's almost time, Kaito.

00:21:54.960 --> 00:21:56.480
Huh?!

00:21:59.800 --> 00:22:02.670
A-Ana, you're a BOY?

00:22:03.090 --> 00:22:04.360
That's right.

00:22:04.360 --> 00:22:06.360
Anyway, puzzles sure are interesting.

00:22:06.360 --> 00:22:07.840
I take back what I said!

00:22:09.460 --> 00:22:11.470
A guy. For real?

00:22:12.020 --> 00:22:14.800
And I got to meet lots
of wonderful people.

00:22:14.800 --> 00:22:17.110
Especially YOU, Kaito!

00:22:17.730 --> 00:22:18.390
Hey!

00:22:18.390 --> 00:22:20.980
Wait, that's a guy, a guy.

00:22:22.210 --> 00:22:23.990
Thank you, Kaito.

00:22:26.760 --> 00:22:28.960
-A-A guy...

00:22:37.290 --> 00:22:41.510
Tsukue no ue de umareta sekai
A world born on top of a desk

00:22:41.510 --> 00:22:47.430
Ichiban saki ni kimi ni misetakatta
I wanted to show it to you first of all

00:22:47.430 --> 00:22:52.060
Karappo no heya sotto nukedashite
I sneaked silently out of that empty room

00:22:52.060 --> 00:22:57.110
Hashirihajimeteta
And started running

00:22:58.270 --> 00:23:02.590
Iki hazumasete oka o noboru to
Breathing heavily, I climbed the hill

00:23:02.590 --> 00:23:07.950
Kimi ga saki ni tsuite matte ita ne
And you were already there, waiting

00:23:08.820 --> 00:23:13.130
Takusan no hajimete kimi to mitsuketa
There were so many treasures that I first

00:23:13.130 --> 00:23:18.380
Takaramono datta
Discovered with you

00:23:18.380 --> 00:23:23.720
Kanashisa de afureta toki wa
That time when I was overcome with sadness

00:23:23.720 --> 00:23:26.400
Nanimo iwazu ni tada
You said nothing

00:23:26.400 --> 00:23:29.310
Soba ni ite kureta ne
Just stayed there by my side, didn't you?

00:23:29.310 --> 00:23:33.880
Imademo wasurenai yo
Even now, I haven't forgotten

00:23:33.880 --> 00:23:39.180
Mata aou ne, yakusoku o shiyou
Let's meet again, let's make it a promise

00:23:39.180 --> 00:23:44.460
Kei wa shinai, ano hi no sayonara
It won't fade, the "goodbye" of that day

00:23:44.460 --> 00:23:50.000
Boku no subete, kimi ga kureta michi
Everything I have, the path you gave me

00:23:50.000 --> 00:23:58.940
Zutto kokoro no naka hikaru yo
Will always shine within my heart

00:24:04.300 --> 00:24:06.560
What do you mean,

00:24:06.560 --> 00:24:09.390
"Come with me"?
Those POG guys are up to something, huh?

00:24:09.390 --> 00:24:12.260
That Bishop person is
a bit suspicious, too.

00:24:12.260 --> 00:24:14.380
That smile of his is super fishy.

00:24:14.380 --> 00:24:17.490
When he grins, it makes
everything suspicious, right?

00:24:17.490 --> 00:24:21.350
For example, "Kaito, I made
some sweets for you!" GRIN.

00:24:21.870 --> 00:24:27.250
Invitation from a Nightmare

00:24:21.890 --> 00:24:24.330
Next time: "Invitation from a Nightmare"

00:24:24.330 --> 00:24:27.480
There ain't no puzzle
I can't solve! GRIN.
